From: Marco Martins
Subject: net: bridge: accept turning VLAN filtering off when it is not built

netifd sets IFLA_BR_VLAN_FILTERING on every bridge it creates, also to 0.
Without CONFIG_BRIDGE_VLAN_FILTERING the request failed with -EOPNOTSUPP,
so no bridge could be created: switching off what cannot be on is a no-op.
---
--- a/net/bridge/br_private.h
+++ b/net/bridge/br_private.h
@@ -1741,7 +1741,7 @@
 					unsigned long val,
 					struct netlink_ext_ack *extack)
 {
-	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	return val ? -EOPNOTSUPP : 0;
 }
 
 static inline int nbp_get_num_vlan_infos(struct net_bridge_port *p,
